Instructions
Step 1: Boil & Pound the Taro (Achu)
Boil: Wash the taro thoroughly (keep skins on). Boil in a large pot of water for 45–60 minutes until soft when pierced with a fork. (If using green bananas, boil them alongside the taro).   
Lumo
+ 1

Peel: Peel the taro and bananas while piping hot (warm taro pounds smoothly, whereas cold taro creates hard lumps).   
Lumo

Pound or Process:

Traditional Method: Pound hot taro in a wooden mortar with a pestle until completely smooth and stretchy.   
Lumo

Modern Method: Pulse hot taro in a food processor until smooth and elastic (add a tablespoon of warm water if too stiff).   
Cooking With Claudy

Wrap: Form into smooth balls or logs, wrap tightly in foil, plastic wrap, or warmed banana leaves to retain heat, and set aside.   
Lumo

Step 2: Cook the Proteins & Prepare Broth
Season beef, tripe, cow skin, and smoked fish with salt, pepper, and bouillon cubes.   
Immaculate Bites

Add water and boil until all meats are tender.

Remove meat pieces and set them aside. Reserve 3 to 4 cups of hot, seasoned stock for the soup base.   
Immaculate Bites

Step 3: Make the Yellow Soup (Emulsion)
Warm the Oil: Slightly warm the palm oil in a saucepan for 1 minute. It should be liquid and warm, never hot or bleached.   
Lumo

Emulsify:

Blender Method (Easiest): Pour the warm palm oil into a blender. Add the clear, strained limestone water (kanwa solution). Pulse for a few seconds until the oil emulsifies and turns a bright, thick yellow color.   
Cooking With Claudy
+ 2

Manual Method: Whisk warm palm oil and strained limestone water together vigorously in a clay bowl or pot until thick and yellow.   
Lumo

Add Spices & Stock: Pour the warm meat stock and Achu spice mix into the emulsified yellow base. Blend or whisk until thoroughly mixed, creamy, and uniform.   
Immaculate Bites

Adjust: Taste and adjust with salt, seasoning cube, or pepper as desired.   
Cooking With Claudy

How to Serve & Eat
Mound the Achu: Place a portion of pounded taro onto a large flat plate and shape it into a rounded mound.   
Cooking With Claudy

Make the Well: Press a deep circular well into the middle of the taro mound.   
Cooking With Claudy

Pour Soup & Meat: Ladle the warm yellow soup directly into the central well and place the cooked meats, cow skin, and smoked fish around or inside the soup.   
Cooking With Claudy

To Eat: Clean your hands thoroughly. Use your index finger to scoop a piece of taro dough from the outer rim in a circular motion, dip it into the yellow soup in the center, and enjoy!   
